ing:11px 22px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--mlc-accent);color:#1a1228;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--mlc-accent);transition:filter .15s}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-btn:hover{filter:brightness(1.08);color:#1a1228}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-btns{flex:none;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-btn-2{background:transparent;color:var(--mlc-accent-text)}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-btn-2:hover{background:var(--mlc-card);color:var(--mlc-accent-text)}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-note{margin:10px 0 0;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--mlc-mfg)}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-bullets{margin:0;padding-left:20px;color:var(--mlc-mfg)}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-bullets li{margin:0 0 10px}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-bullets strong{color:var(--mlc-fg)}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-stay,.mlc-wrap .mlc-switch{margin-top:36px}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-stay{padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--mlc-border);border-radius:14px;background:var(--mlc-card)}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-move-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px;margin:18px 0 4px}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-move-grid>div{padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--mlc-border);border-radius:12px;background:var(--mlc-card)}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-move-title{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:1rem}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-also{margin-top:22px;font-size:.95rem;color:var(--mlc-mfg)}\n.mlc-wrap .mlc-panel-hero{margin-top:8px}\n.mlc-wrap a:focus-visible,.mlc-wrap summary:focus-visible,.mlc-wrap .mlc-scroll:focus-visible,.mlc-wrap .mlc-pre:focus-visible,.mlc-wrap .mlc-btn:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--mlc-accent);outline-offset:2px}\n@container (max-width:720px){.mlc-wrap .mlc-codes{grid-template-columns:1fr}.mlc-wrap .mlc-cta{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;padding:20px}}\n@container (max-width:640px){.mlc-wrap .mlc-move-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px}.mlc-wrap .mlc-stay{padding:18px}}\n@container (max-width:560px){.mlc-wrap .mlc-table{min-width:0;font-size:.9rem}.mlc-wrap .mlc-table thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0)}.mlc-wrap .mlc-table,.mlc-wrap .mlc-table tbody,.mlc-wrap .mlc-table tr,.mlc-wrap .mlc-table th,.mlc-wrap .mlc-table td{display:block;width:auto}.mlc-wrap .mlc-table tbody tr{border-bottom:1px solid var(--mlc-border);padding:12px 14px}.mlc-wrap .mlc-table tbody tr:last-child{border-bottom:0}.mlc-wrap .mlc-table tbody th{width:auto;padding:0 0 8px;border:0;font-weight:600;color:var(--mlc-fg)}.mlc-wrap .mlc-table tbody td{width:auto;padding:8px 10px;border:0;border-radius:6px}.mlc-wrap .mlc-table tbody td+td{margin-top:6px;background:var(--mlc-muted)}.mlc-wrap .mlc-table tbody td::before{content:attr(data-mlc-label);display:block;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--mlc-mfg);margin-bottom:2px}.mlc-wrap .mlc-pre{font-size:.74rem;padding:14px}}\n</style>\n<div class=\"mlc-head\"><p class=\"mlc-kicker\">Migration guide</p><h1 class=\"mlc-h2\">Migrate from Cloudinary to MediaLit</h1><p class=\"mlc-lead\">A lot of teams use Cloudinary mostly to take user uploads, make a thumbnail and serve the file. If that&#39;s you, the credit bill can grow faster than the app does. This guide shows how to migrate from Cloudinary: what carries over to MediaLit, what doesn&#39;t, and a script that copies your files across.</p><div class=\"mlc-eyebrow-note\">Written November 2026. If you depend on URL transforms or video streaming, read &ldquo;Stay on Cloudinary if&rdquo; first.</div></div>\n<section class=\"mlc-panel mlc-panel-hero\"><h2 class=\"mlc-h3\">What carries over</h2><p class=\"mlc-intro\">MediaLit does its image work once, when a file is uploaded, and then serves plain files. There is no URL that resizes images on request, so there&#39;s also nothing for someone else to point at your account.</p>\n<div class=\"mlc-table-card\"><div class=\"mlc-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Cloudinary features and their MediaLit equivalents\"><table class=\"mlc-table\"><caption class=\"mlc-sr\">Cloudinary features mapped to MediaLit</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">In Cloudinary</th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"mlc-col-ml\">In MediaLit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Upload API or upload preset</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">Yes: </span><code>POST /media/create</code>, or <code>medialit.upload()</code> in the Node SDK</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Signed uploads from the browser</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">Yes: </span><code>createSignatureHandler</code> on your server plus <code>&lt;MediaLitUploader&gt;</code>. Large files upload in resumable chunks</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>public_id</code></th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">Yes: </span><code>mediaId</code>, assigned by MediaLit</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Folders and tags</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-p\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 8h8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">Partly: </span><code>group</code>, one per file</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>f_auto</code> / WebP delivery</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-p\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 8h8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">Partly: </span>Optional WebP conversion once, at upload, with a quality setting</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Thumbnails</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">Yes: </span>Generated at upload for images and videos</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Private and authenticated delivery</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">Yes: </span>Private files are served through expiring signed URLs</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">On-the-fly URL transforms (<code>w_</code>, <code>c_</code>, effects)</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-n\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4.5 4.5l7 7M11.5 4.5l-7 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">No: </span>Not supported. Generate the sizes you need before or at upload</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Fetch and transform remote URLs</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-n\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4.5 4.5l7 7M11.5 4.5l-7 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">No: </span>Not supported. MediaLit only stores files uploaded with an API key or upload signature</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Video transcoding and adaptive streaming</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-n\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4.5 4.5l7 7M11.5 4.5l-7 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">No: </span>Not supported. Videos are stored and served as uploaded</span></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">AI agents</th><td data-mlc-label=\"MediaLit\"><span class=\"mlc-cell\"><svg class=\"mlc-ic mlc-ic-y\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span><span class=\"mlc-sr\">Yes: </span>MCP server at <code>https://api.medialit.cloud/mcp</code> and a CLI</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>\n\n<h2 class=\"mlc-h3\" style=\"margin-top:44px\">Migrate in five steps</h2>\n<h4 class=\"mlc-h4\">1. Pick a plan that fits your largest file</h4>\n<p class=\"mlc-intro\">Basic is free with 1 GB of storage and a 50 MB file limit. Pro is $10/mo or $100/yr for 100 GB and files up to 2 GB. You can also <a href=\"/docs/self-hosting\">self-host MediaLit</a> on AWS S3, Cloudflare R2 or MinIO with the same API. Create an API key in your app&#39;s settings and turn on WebP conversion there if you want it.</p>\n<h4 class=\"mlc-h4\">2. Copy your files across</h4>\n<p class=\"mlc-intro\">This Node.js script pages through your Cloudinary uploads, copies each original into MediaLit, and writes a map of old <code>public_id</code> to new URL. Downloading the originals counts toward your Cloudinary bandwidth, so run it once, near the start of a billing cycle.</p>\n<div class=\"mlc-codes\" style=\"grid-template-columns:1fr\"><figure class=\"mlc-code\"><figcaption class=\"mlc-code-head\"><span>migrate.mjs</span><span class=\"mlc-chip\">Node.js</span></figcaption><pre class=\"mlc-pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code>import { v2 as cloudinary } from &quot;cloudinary&quot;;\nimport { MediaLit } from &quot;medialit&quot;;\nimport { writeFile } from &quot;node:fs/promises&quot;;\n\ncloudinary.config();             // reads CLOUDINARY_URL\nconst medialit = new MediaLit(); // reads MEDIALIT_API_KEY\nconst map = {};\nlet cursor;\n\ndo {\n  const page = await cloudinary.api.resources({\n    type: &quot;upload&quot;,\n    resource_type: &quot;image&quot;, // run again for &quot;video&quot; and &quot;raw&quot;\n    max_results: 500,\n    next_cursor: cursor,\n  });\n  for (const r of page.resources) {\n    const res = await fetch(r.secure_url);\n    const buffer = Buffer.from(await res.arrayBuffer());\n    const { mediaId } = await medialit.upload(buffer, {\n      access: &quot;public&quot;,\n      fileName: `${r.public_id.split(&quot;/&quot;).pop()}.${r.format}`,\n      group: r.asset_folder || r.folder || undefined,\n    });\n    const media = await medialit.seal(mediaId); // keep it\n    map[r.public_id] = media.file;\n  }\n  cursor = page.next_cursor;\n} while (cursor);\n\nawait writeFile(&quot;cloudinary-map.json&quot;, JSON.stringify(map, null, 2));</code></pre><p class=\"mlc-code-note\">Uploads stay temporary until <code>seal()</code>, and unsealed files are deleted after 24 hours, so a half-finished run doesn&#39;t leave junk behind. Use <code>access: &quot;private&quot;</code> for files that shouldn&#39;t be public.</p></figure></div>\n<h4 class=\"mlc-h4\">3. Switch new uploads</h4>\n<p class=\"mlc-intro\">Replace the Cloudinary upload widget with a signature route and the React uploader. Your API key stays on your server, and the browser only gets a short-lived signature.</p>\n<div class=\"mlc-codes\" style=\"grid-template-columns:1fr\"><figure class=\"mlc-code\"><figcaption class=\"mlc-code-head\"><span>Uploads</span><span class=\"mlc-chip\">Next.js + React</span></figcaption><pre class=\"mlc-pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code>// app/api/medialit/signature/route.ts\nimport { createSignatureHandler } from &quot;medialit&quot;;\n\nexport const POST = createSignatureHandler({\n  authorize: async () =&gt; !!(await getSession()), // your app&#39;s auth\n});\n\n// In your React form\nimport { MediaLitUploader } from &quot;@medialit/react&quot;;\nimport &quot;@medialit/react/styles.css&quot;;\n\n&lt;MediaLitUploader\n  signatureEndpoint=&quot;/api/medialit/signature&quot;\n  onUploadComplete={(media) =&gt; saveUrl(media.file)}\n/&gt;;</code></pre></figure></div>\n<h4 class=\"mlc-h4\">4. Update stored URLs</h4>\n<p class=\"mlc-intro\">Use <code>cloudinary-map.json</code> to rewrite the image URLs in your database. Anywhere you built transform URLs in code, such as <code>/w_300,c_fill/</code>, decide on the sizes you actually show, then use MediaLit&#39;s thumbnail or upload those sizes as separate files.</p>\n<h4 class=\"mlc-h4\">5. Turn Cloudinary off last</h4>\n<p class=\"mlc-intro\">Keep Cloudinary running until your pages load only MediaLit URLs. Search your codebase and database for <code>res.cloudinary.com</code> before you delete the account.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"mlc-h3\" style=\"margin-top:44px\">Stay on Cloudinary if</h2>\n<ul class=\"mlc-bullets\"><li>Your front end builds image sizes and crops in the URL on the fly.</li><li>You need video transcoding, adaptive streaming or AI-based effects.</li><li>Your team uses it as a digital asset manager with search and approvals.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"mlc-intro\">MediaLit is the smaller tool for uploads, thumbnails, private files and agent-generated files. See the <a href=\"/compare-cloudinary\">full MediaLit vs Cloudinary comparison</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"mlc-h3\" style=\"margin-top:44px\">Questions</h2><div class=\"mlc-faq\"><details class=\"mlc-faq-item\"><summary>Is MediaLit a Cloudinary alternative?</summary><p>For uploads, thumbnails, private files and files your AI agents create, yes. For on-the-fly URL transforms, video streaming or asset management, no. See <a href=\"/compare-cloudinary\">MediaLit vs Cloudinary</a>.</p></details><details class=\"mlc-faq-item\"><summary>Can I move from Cloudinary to R2 or S3?</summary><p>Yes. Self-host MediaLit on Cloudflare R2, AWS S3 or MinIO, then run the same script with <code>new MediaLit({ endpoint: &quot;https://your-instance&quot; })</code>. The <a href=\"/docs/self-hosting\">self-hosting guide</a> covers each one.</p></details><details class=\"mlc-faq-item\"><summary>How do I export images from Cloudinary?</summary><p>Page through the Admin API&#39;s <code>resources</code> call and download each <code>secure_url</code>, as the script above does. Run it once per resource type: image, video and raw.</p></details><details class=\"mlc-faq-item\"><summary>Is Cloudinary too expensive for my app?</summary><p>Cloudinary bills in credits shared across storage, bandwidth and transformations. MediaLit bills by storage: Basic is free for 1 GB, and Pro is $10/mo for 100 GB. If you mostly store and serve files, compare your last few Cloudinary invoices against that.</p></details><details class=\"mlc-faq-item\"><summary>Can someone run up my bill with fetch URLs?</summary><p>MediaLit has no feature that fetches and transforms images from other sites. Files only get in through an upload made with your API key or a short-lived upload signature.</p></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"mlc-cta\"><div><p class=\"mlc-cta-title\">Try it with a few files first</p><p class=\"mlc-cta-text\">Basic is free with 1 GB. Run the script on one folder before you move everything.</p></div><div class=\"mlc-btns\"><a class=\"mlc-btn\" href=\"https://app.medialit.cloud/login\">Start free</a><a class=\"mlc-btn mlc-btn-2\" href=\"/docs/quick-start\">Read the docs</a></div></div>\n</section>\n<p class=\"mlc-foot\">Cloudinary API names are from Cloudinary&#39;s public Admin API docs. MediaLit plan limits are from <a href=\"https://medialit.cloud/#pricing\">medialit.cloud</a>. Spotted something out of date? <a href=\"https://github.com/codelitdev/medialit/issues\">Open an issue</a>.</p>\n</div>"
      }
    }
  ]
}
